{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159jum1jD83fZcVn5MVkUrh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd095-nohup\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/nohup: Run a Command Immune to Hangups\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships nohup but the GNU version has specific behavior for stdout/stderr\n6\t  redirection to nohup.out. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n7\t  binary (gnohup, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n8\t  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Run a command immune to SIGHUP, with stdout/stderr redirection when not a terminal.\n12\t  - G2: Verify functional parity against gnohup via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: SIGHUP immunity and output redirection\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must ignore SIGHUP (signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGHUP)) before executing COMMAND.\n20\t      - R1.2:\n21\t          text: If stdout is a terminal, must redirect stdout to nohup.out in the current directory. If that fails, must redirect to $HOME/nohup.out. Must print a message to stderr indicating where output is redirected.\n22\t      - R1.3:\n23\t          text: If stderr is a terminal and stdout has been redirected, must redirect stderr to stdout (i.e., both go to nohup.out).\n24\t      - R1.4:\n25\t          text: Must pass all remaining arguments after COMMAND as arguments to the executed command.\n26\t\n27\t  R2:\n28\t    title: Exit codes\n29\t    items:\n30\t      - R2.1:\n31\t          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n32\t      - R2.2:\n33\t          text: Must exit 125 when nohup itself fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n34\t      - R2.3:\n35\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n36\t\n37\tnon_goals:\n38\t  - cmd/nohup does not implement --help or --version beyond usage on error.\n39\t\n40\tacceptance_criteria:\n41\t  - id: AC1\n42\t    criterion: \"nohup echo hello redirects output to nohup.out when stdout is a terminal, matching gnohup.\"\n43\t    traces:\n44\t      - R1.1\n45\t      - R1.2\n46\t      - R1.4\n47\t  - id: AC2\n48\t    criterion: \"nohup missing-cmd exits 127, matching gnohup.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R2.2\n51\t  - id: AC3\n52\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gnohup passes for all required test cases.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t  - id: AC4\n58\t    criterion: \"cmd/nohup compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R1.2\n62\t      - R1.3\n63\t      - R1.4\n64\t      - R2.1\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t      - R2.3\n67\t\n68\tpackage_contract:\n69\t  imports:\n70\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa4a6316-c705-4442-a3d7-cd7eb24466a9","uuid":"2ba2db14-9f7d-4221-8bce-7189f0b20fcd","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:10:29.234Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5567/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd095-nohup.yaml","content":"id: srd095-nohup\ntitle: \"cmd/nohup: Run a Command Immune to Hangups\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships nohup but the GNU version has specific behavior for stdout/stderr\n  redirection to nohup.out. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gnohup, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations,\n  verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Run a command immune to SIGHUP, with stdout/stderr redirection when not a terminal.\n  - G2: Verify functional parity against gnohup via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: SIGHUP immunity and output redirection\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must ignore SIGHUP (signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGHUP)) before executing COMMAND.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: If stdout is a terminal, must redirect stdout to nohup.out in the current directory. If that fails, must redirect to $HOME/nohup.out. Must print a message to stderr indicating where output is redirected.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: If stderr is a terminal and stdout has been redirected, must redirect stderr to stdout (i.e., both go to nohup.out).\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must pass all remaining arguments after COMMAND as arguments to the executed command.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 125 when nohup itself fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/nohup does not implement --help or --version beyond usage on error.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"nohup echo hello redirects output to nohup.out when stdout is a terminal, matching gnohup.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"nohup missing-cmd exits 127, matching gnohup.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gnohup passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/nohup compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
