{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5567) from the cobbler code generation pipeline. The task is to implement `cmd/nohup/main.go` — a Go reimplementation of GNU `nohup` that runs a command immune to SIGHUP with automatic output redirection. The implementation must satisfy srd095 requirements R1.1-R1.4 (core functionality), with exit code handling from R2.1-R2.3. Only `cmd/nohup/main.go` needs to be created. No test file is required for this task. The code must compile and pass `go vet`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU nohup behavior: ignore SIGHUP, redirect stdout/stderr to nohup.out when connected to terminal\n   - SIGHUP immunity via `signal.Ignore(syscall.SIGHUP)` before exec\n   - Terminal detection via `sys.IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Output redirection: stdout to nohup.out (CWD first, fallback $HOME/nohup.out), stderr to stdout if stderr is terminal\n   - Exit codes: child's exit code on success, 125 for nohup failure, 126 for command found but can't invoke, 127 for command not found\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gnohup` reference binary\n   - 40-line function limit (article E8)\n   - No --help or --version (non-goal in SRD)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd095-nohup.yaml` (read)\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements for nohup\n     - R1.1: Ignore SIGHUP before executing COMMAND\n     - R1.2: Redirect stdout to nohup.out (CWD, fallback $HOME), print message to stderr\n     - R1.3: Redirect stderr to stdout when stderr is terminal and stdout was redirected\n     - R1.4: Pass all remaining arguments to child command\n     - R2.1-R2.3: Exit code handling (child s